her and he  apologized um  do you think that was enough at all  no i don't think it was enough uh he  also has said today that he's forgotten  uh that he was told that chris pincher  um was uh a sort of serial perpetrator  of these events and had undertaken a  formal investigation he said that he had  forgotten well as somebody who has had  many of these cases brought to my door  you don't forget so boris johnson has  throughout this process as found by lord  macdonald who came out and basically  skewered him red-handed for the lies he  didn't know a specific case he didn't  know any cases at all he didn't know of  a formal investigation but all of those  things have proved to be untrue so when  boris johnson says he wished it had been  different that it was a mistake this is  just more boris johnson lies he'd do the  same again in fact i wouldn't be  surprised as he was thinking about  whether he should make him the  chancellor  but it is possible i suppose that you  know boris johnson as he claimed or his  number 10 claim didn't immediately  recall  the briefing that he had is it possible  no it's absolutely not possible i'm  afraid to say you know we all have busy  lives and lots of difficult things and  you know he is the prime minister he  also has hundreds of people who work on  those busy lives for him hundreds of  other advisers to remind him of things  um it's absolutely not true i'm sorry  it's just it's it's  the story has changed so much to the  point that boris johnson has i mean it's  like in a soap opera where you know  they're trying to bring somebody back  from the dead and they have to do it in  a dream sequence that is what they're i  forgot offen uh defenses it doesn't wash  with me  i'm afraid to say because everything  boris johnson has said in the last three  days has been a lie this is a lie as  well what about uh implications for  labor if he does go i mean he's been  polling pretty badly the tories have  been struggling in the polls losing 